class.description:
[AudioMixerServer] plays audio on named channels (for example [code]music[/code], [code]ambience[/code], [code]voice[/code] and [code]sfx[/code]) without nodes, so music keeps playing across [method SceneTree.change_scene_to_file] and the pause menu. Each channel is defined by an [AudioMixerChannel], plays on an existing audio bus, has a queue of streams with a cursor, and supports fades, cross-fades and overlapping one-shots.
Channels come from the [AudioMixerLayout] set in the project setting [code]audio/mixer/default_layout[/code] (loaded on first use), from [method load_layout] or from [method add_channel].
Streams can be given as an [AudioStream] or as a path. Queue entries given as a path are loaded when they start and released when they no longer play, so only the current entry (and, with [member AudioMixerChannel.preload_next], the next one) is kept in memory.
The volume of a voice is its fade gain (see [method get_fade_gain]) times the channel volume (see [method set_channel_volume_db]) times the volume of its bus. The mixer never changes buses or bus volumes.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	var music = AudioMixerChannel.new()
	music.channel_name = &"music"
	music.bus = &"Music"
	music.default_fade_time = 2.0
	music.queue_mode = AudioMixerChannel.QUEUE_MODE_LOOP_QUEUE
	AudioMixerServer.add_channel(music)

	AudioMixerServer.channel_started.connect(_on_channel_started)
	AudioMixerServer.enqueue(&"music", "res://music/title.ogg")
	AudioMixerServer.enqueue(&"music", "res://music/level_1.ogg")
	AudioMixerServer.play(&"music")

func _on_level_started():
	AudioMixerServer.next(&"music") # Cross-fades for 2 seconds.

func _on_channel_started(channel, index, stream_path):
	print("%s plays entry %d: %s" % [channel, index, stream_path])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
	var music = new AudioMixerChannel();
	music.ChannelName = "music";
	music.Bus = "Music";
	music.DefaultFadeTime = 2.0f;
	music.QueueMode = AudioMixerChannel.QueueModeEnum.LoopQueue;
	AudioMixerServer.AddChannel(music);

	AudioMixerServer.Singleton.ChannelStarted += OnChannelStarted;
	AudioMixerServer.Enqueue("music", "res://music/title.ogg");
	AudioMixerServer.Enqueue("music", "res://music/level_1.ogg");
	AudioMixerServer.Play("music");
}

private void OnLevelStarted()
{
	AudioMixerServer.Next("music"); // Cross-fades for 2 seconds.
}

private void OnChannelStarted(StringName channel, long index, string streamPath)
{
	GD.Print($"{channel} plays entry {index}: {streamPath}");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Channels can also be controlled by data: an [AudioCommand] describes one action (play, stop, toggle, fade, enqueue, ...), an [AudioCommandList] holds many and saves as [code].tres[/code], JSON, INI or CSV. [method execute] runs a command; [method register_commands] makes the commands of a list callable by name ([method execute_named]) and by group ([method execute_group]). The project setting [code]audio/mixer/default_commands[/code] registers a list at startup.
[b]Note:[/b] All methods must be called on the main thread, like the playback API of [AudioServer] that the mixer uses. Signals are emitted on the main thread.
[b]Note:[/b] The mixer updates fades, detects the end of streams and advances queues once per frame, when the [AudioServer] updates on the main thread (also while the [SceneTree] is paused). The next queue entry therefore starts up to one frame after the previous one ended. For gapless sequences, put an [AudioStreamPlaylist] into one queue entry.
[b]Note:[/b] On the Web, streams play as samples by default (project setting [code]audio/general/default_playback_type.web[/code]). Fades work for samples too; browsers start audio only after the first user input.

method.description:
Runs the registered command named [param command_name] (see [method register_commands]). Returns [constant ERR_DOES_NOT_EXIST] and prints an error if no command has that name.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# A soundboard button: one TOGGLE command per button.
func _on_pad_pressed(pad_name):
	AudioMixerServer.execute_named(pad_name)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// A soundboard button: one Toggle command per button.
private void OnPadPressed(StringName padName)
{
	AudioMixerServer.ExecuteNamed(padName);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
